      "rationale": "The single-device assumption behind local SQLite doesn't hold: the beta survey shows most hikers already use TrailKeeper on their phone and the web dashboard, and a fifth of them lost photos or edits made on the other device. Postgres with a per-user sync log lets both surfaces read and write the same trip; we accept running one small managed instance in exchange for not losing anyone's trip again.",
